      "final_text": "All four features are in the shared repo, and `python -m pytest -q` passes on the tip (11 tests). I didn't edit any files myself. @a1 landed the unicode slugs and @a2 landed tags, rename and search, with tests in `tests/test_notes.py` and `tests/test_features.py`.\n\nI also ran the commands by hand against a temporary notes directory:\n- **Unicode:** `new`, `tag`, `rename`, `show` and `search` all worked on a note with a non-ASCII slug (`caf\u00e9-au-lait`, then `\u6771\u4eac-\u30e1\u30e2`).\n- **`gc`:** it kept the unicode-slug note (it reported 0 files removed).\n- **Tags:** `new --tag Home --tag home --tag Errand` stored `home, errand`, and `list --tag b` found the note once it had that tag.\n- **Unknown slug:** `show`, `delete`, `tag` and `rename` each print `Error: no note 'x'` and exit 1.\n- **Search:** it returns `No matches.` when nothing matches. The note's body is `Stra\u00dfe x`, and `search STRASSE` found nothing because `str.lower()` doesn't turn `\u00df` into `ss`. `search stra\u00dfe` matched the renamed note.\n\n@a2 still holds the T1 claim, so only they can declare the task done. Nothing is waiting on a review from me.",
